+
+config NEBULAOS_BACKLIGHT_PROBE_DIAG
+	bool "NebulaOS bounded backlight PWM/GPIO probe diagnostic (DISPLAY-B0-DIAG)"
+	depends on PWM
+	default n
+	help
+	  Display hardware analysis mission follow-on (2026-08-01+): a
+	  bounded, self-restoring, kernel-owned diagnostic for discovering
+	  the real candidate backlight PWM channel/enable-GPIO electrical
+	  behavior on this board without external measurement equipment,
+	  through a tightly-scoped debugfs command interface exposing
+	  EXACTLY 9 fixed literal commands and nothing else - status, arm,
+	  disarm, probe-enable-low, probe-enable-high, probe-pwm-25,
+	  probe-pwm-50, probe-pwm-75, restore - each taking zero arguments
+	  (command-interface hardening pass, 2026-08-xx: any trailing
+	  argument, e.g. a caller-supplied GPIO/channel number, duty cycle,
+	  period, or timeout, is rejected outright, not silently ignored).
+	  There is no channel/GPIO-number argument at all - only the one
+	  candidate PWM channel and one candidate enable-GPIO this DT node
+	  names can ever be touched. Never touches PWM/GPIO state at boot or
+	  module bind time - probing requires an explicit "arm" command
+	  first (disarmed at every boot), restoration is armed (kernel
+	  workqueue timer scheduled) BEFORE the one candidate hardware write
+	  is ever made, and every probe auto-restores after a FIXED 2-second
+	  timeout (hard maximum 3s, enforced by a build-time static_assert -
+	  there is no caller-supplied timeout argument to bound at runtime
+	  because none can be constructed through this interface at all).
+	  Rejects 0% and 100% duty-cycle requests outright - only
+	  probe-pwm-25/50/75 exist.
+
+	  PWM-exactness gate: a probe is also refused (-EOPNOTSUPP) unless
+	  the specific resource's restoration path is confirmed exact right
+	  now, via a genuine, live query - never a hardcoded answer. For the
+	  candidate enable-GPIO this is always true when the DT property is
+	  present (this board's pinctrl-ingenic.c reads live hardware on
+	  every call). For the candidate PWM channel this now calls the
+	  exported ingenic_pwm_channel_get_state_is_exact() from
+	  pwm-ingenic-v2.c (see CONFIG_PWM_INGENIC_V2_GET_STATE below) for
+	  the exact channel about to be touched; when that option is not
+	  selected, or the query is otherwise unavailable, the gate
+	  conservatively reports "not exact" and refuses the probe - the
+	  fallback is always "refuse to arm", never "assume exact". See
+	  nebulaos_backlight_probe_diag.c's file header and the debugfs
+	  .../status pwm_restore_is_exact / gpio_restore_is_exact fields,
+	  which report this driver's own live answer to the same query.
+
+	  Disabled by default - never enable for a production/active-slot
+	  build until live hardware testing confirms the candidate PWM
+	  channel/enable-GPIO behavior. If unsure, say N.
